+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes pickup reminders, or proposes sending them by email to save the SMS cost. The day before pickup,
+larder reminds each member by SMS that their pantry order is ready. Reminders go by SMS, at about 40 euros a month,
+because a trial of email reminders in 2025 doubled missed pickups; written after a volunteer became the third that year to
+propose switching to email.
+
+## Sending
+
+`remind` in `larder/reminders.py` sends the reminder the day before the pickup slot, on the channel `CHANNEL` names:
+`"sms"`. The email branch remains in the code but no setting turns it on.
+
+## Why SMS, not email
+
+SMS costs about 40 euros a month; email is free. From April to June 2025 reminders went by email. The email
+provider's report showed 34% of the reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry
+orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a bag packed for nothing, and the fresh food in it is thrown away at closing
+time. Many members share one phone across the family and never check email, but they see an SMS.
+
+Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. The proposal came up
+again in issue 52 (`notes/issue-52.md`), and the maintainers kept SMS. A new proposal to switch has to answer these
+numbers.
